/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flowsheetDict  --  pipe05_herschelbulkley_clay_slurry

  A single PIPE carrying the book's yield-pseudoplastic clay slurry (rho 1500 kg/m3, tau_0 = 17 Pa,
  m = 0.83 Pa s^n, n = 0.5) at 0.5 m/s through 500 m of 40 mm pipe.  The flow curve is the
  property dictionary's: the ROWS (constant/experiments/herschelBulkleyEx33.dat, kind adopted),
  interpolated log-log between them, with the YIELD STRESS a datum of its own
  (`yieldStress { value 17 Pa; how ... }`, R8: never read off a fit).  The pipe solves
  eq. 3.46 on the table's own inverse: the wall stress that carries the flow, the plug radius
  R_p = (tau_0/tau_w) R.

  ANCHOR.  The book prints (p. 122-123): phi = tau_0/tau_w = 0.58, tau_w = 29.31 Pa,
  -dP = 1.46e6 Pa, plug velocity 0.62 m/s, plug radius 11.6 mm.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        L1;
        type        pipe;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( delivered );

        operation
        {
            geometry
            {
                D          0.04  m;
                L          500.0  m;
                roughness  4.6e-5  m;
                dz         0.0  m;
            }
        }
    }
);
